config COURSE_REFUSAL_REASON
	bool "Report what the bootloader saw in an image before it judged it"
	depends on BOOT_IMAGE_ACCESS_HOOKS
	help
	  Print four observable facts about a candidate image before MCUboot
	  decides whether to accept it: whether it has an image header, whether
	  it has a TLV area, whether it carries a signature, and whether that
	  signature names the key compiled into this bootloader.

	  MCUboot itself reports only that an image is not valid. It never says
	  why, because bootutil_img_validate() returns a single fih_ret with no
	  cause attached. That is fault injection hardening rather than an
	  oversight: one return value is harder to skip past with a glitch than
	  a set of them.

	  This hook does not change that decision and must never appear to. It
	  reports and then returns FIH_BOOT_HOOK_REGULAR, so MCUboot performs
	  its normal validation and makes every accept and reject call.

if COURSE_REFUSAL_REASON

config COURSE_REFUSAL_REASON_SLOT_OFFSET
	hex "Second offset to look for an image header"
	default 0x1000
	help
	  Swap using offset places a downloaded image one flash sector into the
	  secondary slot rather than at its start. MCUboot knows that offset
	  from its own swap state, but boot_image_check_hook() is handed only an
	  image index and a slot number, so this code has to find the image on
	  its own.

	  It looks for the image magic at the start of the slot first, then
	  here. The value is the erase sector size of the flash device, which is
	  4096 bytes on the ESP32-C6.

endif # COURSE_REFUSAL_REASON
